    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading this page",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Budget remaining** is the number that matters for decisions. Above zero there is room to ship risky changes; at zero, the error-budget policy in `docs/slo.md` applies.\n\n**Burn rate** is what the alerts watch. A spike in the 5m line alone is noise; it pages only when the 1h line agrees. That pairing is what lets the page fire within minutes of a real problem and clear within minutes of the fix.\n\nThe API objectives are measured at the gateway, so they include requests the API never saw \u2014 the 503 when no replica was ready is exactly the failure an in-process metric would miss."
      },
